Skip fakeroot in cpio()/uncpio() when already running as real root

fakeroot exists so a non-root build can fake device-node creation and
arbitrary ownership inside an archive. This dispatcher container runs
lava-run as real root already (confirmed: every dispatcher process is
uid 0), so those syscalls already succeed for real -- fakeroot buys
nothing here.

It's also actively harmful: fakeroot's faked-sysv daemon busy-loops at
~100% CPU in this environment on every cpio() and uncpio() call
(reproduced directly, outside LAVA entirely: `find . -print0 |
fakeroot-sysv cpio --create ...` against a 5GB tree never completed in
20s on an otherwise-idle 4-core host). Confirmed live against a real
qemu health check job (job 6, run with zero other jobs competing for
CPU) still blowing append-overlays' 60s timeout on this alone. Worse,
the orphaned faked-sysv process outlives the job that spawned it --
subprocess.run() here has no timeout=, so LAVA's own action-level
Timeout can raise past a blocked call without ever killing the child,
permanently stealing a CPU core until the container restarts. This
also explains jobs stuck "Running" forever with no abort at all: once
enough orphaned faked-sysv processes accumulate, the dispatcher's own
watchdog can't get scheduled to fire.

--- a/lava_dispatcher/utils/compression.py	2026-09-05 19:21:42.762890930 +0000
+++ b/lava_dispatcher/utils/compression.py	2026-09-05 19:21:42.775877731 +0000
@@ -133,7 +133,13 @@
